# NRG Bloom 301 Redirects
# Old site structure -> New site structure
#
# NOTE ON SHADOWING: Netlify serves a matching static file BEFORE it
# evaluates a non-forced redirect rule. A rule whose source path has a
# corresponding .html file in this repo will never fire unless it is
# forced with "301!". Before adding a rule here, check whether
# <source>.html exists. If it does, either delete the file or force the
# rule. This is why /team and /partnership sat at 200 for months despite
# having rules below.

/energy              /strategy           301
/impact/problem-flared-gas-nigeria      /esg-impact    301
/impact/electricity-opportunity-nigeria  /esg-impact    301
/impact/bitcoin-mining                  /strategy      301
/team                /about-leadership   301
/faq                 /investor-relations 301
/about               /about-leadership   301
/for-investors       /investor-relations 301
/blog                /insights           301
/index.html          /                   301!

# Legacy Webflow bio URLs. Confirmed 404 on 2026-08-06 while Search
# Console showed Google still sending clicks to them over the prior six
# months (/team/makir-volcy 9 clicks, /team/jordane-volcy 3 clicks).
# Specific rules first, then a catch-all for any other /team/ child.
/team/makir-volcy    /makir-volcy        301
/team/julie-peeters  /julie-peeters      301
/team/jordane-volcy  /jordane-volcy      301
/team/gus-anyim      /gus-anyim          301
/team/*              /about-leadership   301

# Founder decision 2026-08-06: /partnership cannibalised /energy-partners
# for the same partner queries and earned zero clicks in six months of
# Search Console data. partnership.html is deleted so this rule fires.
/partnership         /energy-partners    301

# /facts-and-numbers retired 2026-08-06 by founder decision. It was an
# investor deck served at a public URL; the confidentiality pass stripped it
# and the founder then removed the page entirely. Redirected to
# /investor-relations, the topically adjacent page, which now carries the
# gated investor-pack request form. Adjacency matters: Google treats a 301 to
# an unrelated page as a soft 404 and passes no link equity. Both the clean
# URL and the legacy .html form are covered, since Google indexed both.
/facts-and-numbers        /investor-relations   301
/facts-and-numbers.html   /investor-relations   301

# Retired Webflow template leftovers, deleted 2026-08-06. They were never
# linked from a real page and had no search value. Sent to the nearest
# live equivalent rather than left to 404.
/search              /insights           301
/detail_blog         /insights           301
/detail_team         /about-leadership   301
/detail_impact       /esg-impact         301
/detail_services     /strategy           301
/detail_resources    /insights           301
/template/*          /                   301

# /contact -> /discuss-partnership was REMOVED 2026-08-06. contact.html is
